      "text": "To find the value of the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), let's first observe the pattern in the sequence of numbers. The series alternates between two positive numbers and two negative numbers.\n\nHere's what the sequence looks like:\n\\[1, -4, 7, -10, 13, -16, 19, -22, 25, -28, \\ldots, 55\\]\n\nWe can group the terms into pairs in a way that simplifies the calculation:\n\\[\n(1 - 4) + (7 - 10) + (13 - 16) + (19 - 22) + \\cdots + (49 - 52) + 55\n\\]\n\nEach pair simplifies to \\(-3\\) or \\(3\\) (starting from \\(1 - 4 = -3\\), \\(7 - 10 = -3\\), and so on):\n\\[(-3) + (-3) + (-3) + (-3) + \\cdots + (-3) + 55\\]\n\nThe number of pairs is equal to the total number of terms minus one, since the sequence ends with \\(55\\), which is not paired with anything. The number of terms in the sequence from \\(1\\) to \\(55\\) is \\(28\\), so there are \\(27\\) terms left unpaired. Therefore, there are \\(27\\) pairs.\n\nThe value of each pair is \\(-3\\), so the total value from all pairs is:\n\\[27 \\times (-3) = -81\\]\n\nNow, we add the unpaired term \\(55\\) to the total value of the pairs:\n\\[-81 + 55 = -26\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\\boxed{-26}\\]",
