      "text": "To find the value of the given expression carefully and systematically, let's break down the pattern and perform calculations step by step. \n\nGiven expression:\n\\[ 1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55 \\]\n\nNotice that the series alternates between adding and subtracting terms. Let's separate the part where we sum positive numbers and the part where we subtract them.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n#### Summing Series 1: \\( 1, 7, 13, \\ldots, 55 \\)\nThe series is \\( 1, 7, 13, \\ldots, 55 \\).\n\nThis series follows the pattern:\n- The first term \\( a_1 \\) = 1\n- The common difference \\( d \\) = 6 (since \\( 7 - 1 = 6 \\), \\( 13 - 7 = 6 \\), etc.)\n\nWe need to find out how many terms there are. Since we also know the last term \\( l \\) (which is 55), we can determine the number of terms \\( n \\):\n\n\\[ l = a_n = a_1 + (n-1) \\cdot d \\]\n\\[ 55 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 55 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 6n = 55 + 6 - 1 \\]\n\\[ 6n = 60 \\]\n\\[ n = 10 \\]\n\nSo, there are 10 terms in sequence, and since they are odd-indexed, their sum is:\n\\[ S_1 = \\sum_{k=0}^{4} (1 + 6k) \\]\n\\[ S_1 = 1 + (1 + 6\\cdot1) + (1 + 6\\cdot2) + (1 + 6\\cdot3) + (1 + 6\\cdot4) \\]\n\\[ S_1 = 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + 25 \\]\n\\[ S_1 = 75 \\]\n\n#### Subtracting Series 2: \\( 4, 10, 16, \\ldots, 52 \\)\nThe series is \\( 4, 10, 16, \\ldots, 52 \\).\n\nThis series follows the pattern:\n- The first term \\( a_1 \\) = 4\n- The common difference \\( d \\) = 6 (since \\( 10 - 4 = 6 \\), \\( 16 - 10 = 6 \\), etc.)\n\nAgain, let's find the number of terms in this sequence using similar logic:\n\\[ l = a_n = a_1 + (n-1) \\cdot d \\]\n\\[ 52 = 4 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 52 = 4 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 6n = 52 + 6 - 4 \\]\n\\[ 6n = 54 \\]\n\\[ n = 9 \\]\nThere are 9 terms in sequence.\n\nSince they are even-indexed, their sum is:\n\\[ S_2 = \\sum_{k=0}^{4} 4 + 6k \\]\n\\[ S_2 = 4 + (4 + 6 \\cdot 1) + (4 + 6 \\cdot 2) + (4 + 6 \\cdot 3) + (4 + 6 \\cdot 4) \\]\n\\[ S_2 = 4 + 10 + 14 + 18 + 22 \\]\n\\[ S_2 = 78 \\]\n\n#### Combining Sums\nNow, we combine the results computed for \\( S_1 \\) and \\( S_2 \\):\n\\[ Total = S_1 - S_2 \\]\n\\[ Total = 75 - 78 \\]\n\\[ Total = -3 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{-3} \\]",
